{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "k8s-troubleshoot-demo-2024",
    "name": "K8s Troubleshooting Demo",
    "description": "# Kubernetes Troubleshooting with Postman\n\nThis collection demonstrates how to use Postman for troubleshooting Kubernetes deployments.\n\n## Quick Start\n1. Start minikube: `minikube start`\n2. Get the service URL: `minikube service demo-api-service -n demo --url`\n3. Update the `baseUrl` variable with the URL\n4. Run the collection!\n\n## Scenarios\n- **Health Checks**: Verify service health\n- **API Tests**: Test business logic\n- **Troubleshooting**: Find and diagnose issues",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:30080",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "🏥 Health Checks",
      "description": "Essential health check endpoints used by Kubernetes probes",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness Check (/health)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Test: Status code should be 200",
                  "pm.test('Health check returns 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Test: Response indicates healthy",
                  "pm.test('Status is healthy', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('healthy');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Test: Response time is acceptable (under 500ms)",
                  "pm.test('Response time < 500ms', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(500);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Log which pod responded",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "console.log('✅ Pod responded: ' + json.pod);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Kubernetes Liveness Probe endpoint. If this fails, K8s restarts the pod."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness Check (/ready)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Test: Status code should be 200",
                  "pm.test('Readiness check returns 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Test: App is ready",
                  "pm.test('App is ready', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.ready).to.be.true;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Test: Database is connected",
                  "pm.test('Database connection present', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.database).to.exist;",
                  "    pm.expect(json.database).to.not.eql('invalid-host');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Log details",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "console.log('✅ Pod: ' + json.pod + ', DB: ' + json.database);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ready",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["ready"]
            },
            "description": "Kubernetes Readiness Probe endpoint. If this fails, K8s removes the pod from service."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "📊 API Endpoints",
      "description": "Core business API endpoints",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get App Info",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Has required fields', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('name');",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('version');",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('pod');",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('environment');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Version is 1.0.0', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.version).to.eql('1.0.0');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Store pod name for later use",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('lastPod', json.pod);",
                  "console.log('📍 Responded by pod: ' + json.pod);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/info",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "info"]
            },
            "description": "Returns application information including which pod is responding."
          },
          "response": []
        },
